39535823 17592186045443 true] [17592186530578 1080 "k=3" 13194139535823 17592186045443 true] [17592186530578 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535823 17592186045443 true] [17592186530578 1083 #uuid "b571ca6d-4ec5-50fd-8827-bb0c6a423d56" 13194139535823 17592186045443 true] [17592186530579 1068 #edb/ref 17592186530574 13194139535823 17592186045443 true] [17592186530579 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535823 17592186045443 true] [17592186530579 1071 "If $kA=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & -54 & 60\\end{bmatrix}$,\nwhere $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$" 13194139535823 17592186045443 true] [17592186530579 1072 #uuid "f16bbe6e-f1a6-54a1-bc2e-dc02da0cf210" 13194139535823 17592186045443 true] [17592186530579 1074 "To express $kA,$ we multiply each entry of $A$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}- 2 k & - 9 k & 10 k\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kA$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}- 2 k & - 9 k & 10 k\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & -54 & 60\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the elements in row $1$ and column $2$, $- 9 k$ and $-54.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 9 k & =-54 \\\\ k & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." 13194139535823 17592186045443 true] [17592186530580 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186059741.py" 13194139535823 17592186045443 true] [17592186530580 1169 #uuid "b3722823-efb6-5ebe-bf0d-534c30b694f8" 13194139535823 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"2cb42f95-4419-5a51-91ab-4d7c28e0f3b0" 17592186530573 "71c0ea85-8283-576a-8299-6ae94d64a63b" 17592186530574 "7437b57a-2a12-5152-9852-a33567178cc2" 17592186530575 "8dcd8fd2-48c4-5255-ac9e-25c8